1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:04,421
[BILLY] <i>You have a lot to explain, Abi.</i>

2
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:07,632
<i>How did you get your hands</i>
<i>on our LoveFeast concept?</i>

3
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:08,925
[ABI] <i>Your concept?</i>

4
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:12,178
<i>Don't take what's mine, Ms. Billy.</i>

5
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,180
[BILLY]<i> You messed with</i>
<i>the wrong person.</i>

6
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:18,018
<i>And I will make sure you face</i>
<i>the consequences.</i>

7
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:22,188
<i>Girls, I'm so sorry.</i>
<i>I know it's the weekend.</i>

8
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:24,482
<i>But we need to have a meeting tomorrow.</i>

9
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:27,027
[YANI] <i>This will be my best series yet.</i>

10
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:29,237
<i>We'll make a lot of sales.</i>

11
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,530
<i>What's in that?</i>

12
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>A lot of things.</i>

13
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:36,244
<i>Even the list of investors is in here.</i>

14
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:39,039
<i>Billy said I was a thief.</i>

15
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,207
<i>But she's the original thief herself!</i>

16
00:00:41,291 --> 00:00:45,003
<i>I'll find something I can use</i>
<i>against this woman.</i>

17
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:48,089
[PRECIOUS]
<i>Maybe you should stay away from her.</i>

18
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:51,301
[BILLY] <i>If we let it slide,</i>
<i>then she'll do it again.</i>

19
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,303
<i>She messed with the wrong person.</i>

20
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:56,181
[DRAMATIC MUSIC BUILDS, THEN FADES]

21
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,605
[SOFT FOOTSTEPS]

22
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:10,945
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

23
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,620
Billy…

24
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:22,082
Hi!

25
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:24,000
Sorry, I woke you up.

26
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:26,252
[BILLY SIGHS]

27
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,505
Can I crash beside you tonight?

28
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:29,756
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

29
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,591
- No.
- What do you mean, "no"?

30
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:34,302
- No, no! No, no, no, no!
- No choice! Slide over!

31
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:35,428
[WHINING] Not allowed!

32
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,263
- And why am I not allowed here?
- Come on, Billy!

33
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:39,015
- Because…
- What?

34
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:41,017
- Because…
- Because…?

35
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,894
- Just because.
- Let's share the bed, okay?

36
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:44,103
- No…
- All right, back to sleep.

37
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:45,146
Good night!

38
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:47,232
- Good night.
- [ANNOYED] Good night.

39
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:48,608
[GIGGLES]

40
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:52,237
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

41
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,239
[MUSIC FADING]

42
00:01:55,198 --> 00:02:01,037
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:39,951
[DISTANT BIRDS CHIRPING]

44
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:40,994
[BILLY] Oliver?

45
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,538
I'm sorry, I can't be with you right now.

46
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:44,789
I promise, I'll make it up to you.

47
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:46,833
Next time, we'll go together.

48
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:48,001
Okay, Billy.

49
00:02:48,084 --> 00:02:49,377
Yes, ma'am.

50
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:52,547
Don't worry, Billy.
You can leave him to me.

51
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:57,635
- Hello!
- Uh…

52
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,429
Sir, we're here for the boxing class.

53
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:00,597
His name's Oliver Cariño.

54
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,223
You came right on time, ma'am.

55
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:03,516
The class is about to begin.

56
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,767
- Let's go, Oliver.
- Okay.

57
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:13,943
Precious?

58
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:16,988
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:03:17,071 --> 00:03:18,072
Brandon?

60
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,032
Wow.

61
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:20,909
What a coincidence.

62
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,368
[SOFTLY] Yeah.

63
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:25,872
It's really nice to meet you.

64
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:27,123
At last.

65
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:32,712
[FLASH DRIVE CLICKING]

66
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:38,885
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:39,802
[LINE RINGING]

68
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,846
Ms. Camille! [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

69
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,890
I just called to let you know

70
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:47,143
that I've already made a list
of potential investors

71
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,354
so LoveFeast can move forward.

72
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:53,942
I was thinking maybe we should
reach out to them

73
00:03:54,025 --> 00:03:55,693
as soon as possible.

74
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:57,654
Still working on the weekend?

75
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:59,656
Well, same here.

76
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:02,283
We're very much alike in that sense.

77
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:03,284
And I like it.

78
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,327
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

79
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,246
That's just how I am, Ms. Camille.

80
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:09,082
Especially when I really love my job.

81
00:04:09,165 --> 00:04:10,250
Well, keep it up.

82
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:12,502
Yes. I promise.

83
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:15,922
Abi, you're really something else.

84
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:16,965
I'm impressed.

85
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:19,884
Honestly, I should thank you.

86
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:23,554
For being the only one who appreciates me.

87
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:24,681
Thank you.

88
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,475
Just stay in Pebblng, all right?

89
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:29,394
Don't ever go back to Billy.

90
00:04:29,477 --> 00:04:31,312
What? Absolutely not!

91
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:34,023
I'm not going back there.
I don't like her.

92
00:04:35,191 --> 00:04:36,859
I'll never leave.

93
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,278
I'm yours.

94
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:39,362
Only yours.

95
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,989
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:42,532
Thank you, thank you!

97
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:43,950
Thank you!

98
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:51,457
Mr. and Mrs. Chan-Li of Chan-Li Couture
were very responsive.

99
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:54,127
They said they were willing
to set up a meeting with us.

100
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:57,922
Same with Ms. Grace of the House of Gems.

101
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:02,135
We just need to give them
something worth their investment.

102
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,595
Something like LoveFeast?

103
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:06,931
Bigger and better.

104
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,933
Mmm, wait. How about

105
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:11,269
a shopping spree kind of date?

106
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,271
[BILLY] Charm, that's not sustainable.

107
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:15,481
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,983
What if…

109
00:05:17,066 --> 00:05:19,652
I feature LoveListers in my vlog?

110
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,779
Not LoveList-centric.

111
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:24,282
[MARJ] Chief, how about this?

112
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:27,368
What if we offer a honeymoon package?

113
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,328
[CHARM] Mmm!

114
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:32,123
It'll come out wrong if it's not
attached to the wedding package,

115
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:34,584
- which Pebblng stole from us.
- [PHONE RINGS]

116
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:35,752
I'm sorry.

117
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:37,086
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

118
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:39,297
It'll look like we're just pushing for sex

119
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:42,633
rather than finding
the right one at the right time.

120
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:43,843
[PHONE RINGS]

121
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:46,763
Look.

122
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:49,182
They don't own the wedding gimmick.

123
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:51,809
- We just really need a great idea.
- [PHONE RINGS]

124
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,770
- And we need to focus.
- [RINGING CONTINUES]

125
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:56,606
[MUSIC BECOMES BRAZEN]

126
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:57,815
Toni.

127
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,567
Would you like to answer that first?

128
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,280
Girls, look.

129
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:07,533
I know it's the weekend
and you're working.

130
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:08,785
Thank you.

131
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:11,621
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- Let's just regroup on Monday.

132
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:14,874
But please make sure
you have better ideas on the table.

133
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,250
Thank you.

134
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:20,421
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

135
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:22,090
[CHARM] Hey.

136
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:26,094
Didn't you tell Yani
you can't go to his exhibit?

137
00:06:27,136 --> 00:06:29,347
I said I'd be there later.

138
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,641
Our chief is already frustrated, Toni.

139
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:32,725
Yeah.

140
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,228
I wonder how we can possibly help.

141
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:38,898
Geez, she's on the verge of snapping.

142
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,733
And when she's angry, things get ugly.

143
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,151
[VALERIE SCOFFS]

144
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:43,444
I know, right?

145
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:45,947
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CHARM SIGHS]

146
00:06:52,703 --> 00:06:54,497
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,623
Dude.

148
00:06:58,167 --> 00:06:59,210
Hey.

149
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:02,588
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

150
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:04,340
What are you doing here?

151
00:07:04,423 --> 00:07:05,550
It's the weekend.

152
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:16,144
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,437
[PICTURE FRAME THUDS]

154
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:26,279
[MARIELA] It's Saturday.
Where are you going?

155
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:29,115
My boss is asking me to come to work.

156
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:37,039
Like I told you, Ma, I'll be like Abi.

157
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:39,876
I'll be someone great.

158
00:07:40,751 --> 00:07:45,673
I'll be someone successful
whom everyone admires.

159
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:48,009
I'm almost there.

160
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:49,385
Just wait.

161
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:55,016
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,353
Coach, have them warm up first.

163
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:00,480
- Sure.
- Thank you.

164
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,357
Okay, guys.

165
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:05,359
- It's destiny, isn't it?
- [COACH] Six, five, four.

166
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:07,403
- Huh?
- Three, two, go.

167
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:10,072
That you enrolled your child here.

168
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:13,910
In our messages,
you said you adopted two kids.

169
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:18,706
Ah, yes.
Oliver and his older sister, Billy.

170
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,751
Billy is the CEO of LoveList.

171
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:27,256
- Wow! I should thank her.
- [SOFT LAUGH]

172
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,591
Uh…

173
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:31,177
So you teach children?

174
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,513
Does that mean you're good with kids?

175
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:35,223
Like, you're patient with them?

176
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:37,475
Well, I love kids.

177
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:41,354
I'm the eldest of ten stubborn siblings.

178
00:08:42,688 --> 00:08:45,983
I help take care of them.

179
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:49,278
I also help with their education.

180
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,364
Is that why you never got to marry?

181
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:52,490
Single.

182
00:08:53,324 --> 00:08:54,534
- And ready to--
- [LAUGHS]

183
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,619
They're waiting for you. Look!

184
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:01,582
Uh, all right, but can you join me?

185
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,125
- Huh? Oh, no, no, no.
- Will that be okay?

186
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,544
- Come on, Precious.
- I don't know how.

187
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,630
It won't take long, it's just the warm-up.
Look, we're lacking one participant.

188
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:10,132
Come on. It's just the warm-up.
This will be quick.

189
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:11,759
- Okay, okay.
- Huh?

190
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:14,178
- Yes. Okay.
- Thank you, thank you!

191
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:18,641
So is everyone okay now? Let's start?

192
00:09:19,392 --> 00:09:23,354
Okay, so what's important in boxing
is to give and take.

193
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:27,066
Okay? Okay, all right. Face your partner.

194
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:29,569
- Boxing stance.
- [PRECIOUS] Shh, shh, shh!

195
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,530
Put your hands up first like this, yes.

196
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:35,950
Okay, we'll do it first.
Boxing stance, okay?

197
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,034
Jab…

198
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:39,453
then straight.

199
00:09:40,037 --> 00:09:43,749
Okay? Again, jab and straight.

200
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:48,671
Okay? For the next one,
we'll go forward and backward.

201
00:09:48,754 --> 00:09:49,797
Forward…

202
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:52,633
then backward.

203
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,260
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

204
00:09:54,343 --> 00:09:55,803
[SOFT PUNCHES LANDING]

205
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,179
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

206
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:03,352
Her friends' accounts are also locked.

207
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:07,189
I assume those are troll accounts.

208
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:11,777
Maybe she did that
just in case you check her socials.

209
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:14,655
I can't let this pass anymore, Jordan.

210
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,451
I remember this.

211
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:21,203
She said she owns an internet cafe.

212
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,332
But is that true?

213
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:25,458
She could be lying.

214
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:29,003
Then I'll visit the place!

215
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:31,672
- So we can be sure.
- Uh, Chief.

216
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:34,425
I'll do it. I volunteer.

217
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:36,177
Me too! I'll come.

218
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:39,597
Count me in!

219
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:41,932
Count me in!

220
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:47,146
- [ADMIRING GASP]
- How do I look?

221
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:49,315
Wow!

222
00:10:49,398 --> 00:10:51,359
You're so pretty! You've become more--

223
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,903
more beautiful, Ms. Camille!

224
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,112
Thank you.

225
00:10:56,113 --> 00:10:57,239
Anyway…

226
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,867
What are the basis of your assumptions

227
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:03,245
that they're interested in investing
in a dating company like ours?

228
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:05,164
It's pretty basic, Ms. Camille.

229
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:09,168
All of those businesses
will benefit from LoveFeast.

230
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:13,172
Fashion. Beauty and wellness. Self-care.

231
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:15,925
Like Ms. Lindsay's skincare brand.

232
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:19,595
Okay. Set up a meeting with them ASAP.

233
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:23,974
And tell Morrie first thing by Monday to
draft the proposal and send it right away.

234
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:27,186
Ah! Yes, I'll do that immediately. Noted!

235
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:28,854
What are you waiting for?

236
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:30,398
Try on those clothes.

237
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:31,857
Ms. Camille?

238
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:36,445
These? These are all mine?

239
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:40,032
- Thank-- Thank you…
- Abi.

240
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:42,326
You're working for me now.

241
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:45,037
You're representing Pebblng.

242
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:48,666
I can't have you looking like that.

243
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,335
You must look the part.

244
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:54,338
And, honestly…

245
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:58,217
The only thing I like about this
are your shoes.

246
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:01,720
So, go. Try those on.

247
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,890
Yes. Thank you.

248
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,392
Ah.
[HANGERS RATTLE]

249
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:08,436
Your bag.

250
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,234
Um…

251
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:17,862
- Ms. Camille?
- Hm?

252
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:24,076
Uh, if it's not too much to ask, could I…

253
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,246
ask for a salary advance?

254
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:31,375
I'm really behind on my bills.

255
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,627
And my mother…

256
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:36,380
She has a checkup later today.

257
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:39,008
[ABI INHALES, HESITATES]

258
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:42,386
I know I'm being shameless right now,

259
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:45,973
but I'm really tight on budget.

260
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:57,193
But it's fine if not.
I'm fine, Ms. Camille.

261
00:12:57,276 --> 00:13:00,112
You shouldn't be worrying
about my problems, right?

262
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,907
I was just kidding. I'll try these on now.

263
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:05,117
Okay.

264
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,540
Eh? It's closed now.

265
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,711
Hey! But the computers are still here.

266
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,630
[CHARM] Uh, wait, let's call them.

267
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:21,091
- Hello, Ms. Tere?
- Hello, Abi!

268
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:23,886
I'll pay off my debts to you.

269
00:13:23,969 --> 00:13:26,180
I'll open my internet cafe again.

270
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:30,267
I'll pay my debts in full,
so wait for me, okay?

271
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:34,396
You'll pay? You got money now?
I don't believe you.

272
00:13:35,356 --> 00:13:36,774
I told you, I have money!

273
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:38,651
And my computers aren't yours yet,

274
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:41,403
so just wait there 'cause
I'm taking them all back, okay?

275
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:43,656
I'm on my way. Wait for me.

276
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:44,823
Okay.

277
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,662
- [LINE RINGING]
- Ah, hello?

278
00:13:49,745 --> 00:13:54,750
We'd like to inquire about
the Click Station internet cafe.

279
00:13:56,335 --> 00:14:01,423
- Is this shop Abi's?
- Yeah! That's Abi's!

280
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:02,508
Hello?

281
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:04,802
How's it going? Did you find it?

282
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:07,054
Yes, but it's closed now.

283
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:10,558
[CHARM] It's closed only because
she has debts to the landlady.

284
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,810
The landlady's holding
all her computer units.

285
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:16,105
But the landlady said Abi's going to pay

286
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:19,483
and take back the shop and her computers.

287
00:14:20,317 --> 00:14:22,236
She won't take anything back.

288
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,238
What?

289
00:14:24,321 --> 00:14:28,951
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:30,786
Okay, Oliver, last five seconds!

291
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:36,750
Five, four, three, two, one!
That's awesome!

292
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:41,630
Good job, kids. Let's resume
in our next session, okay?

293
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,215
Thank you and see you!

294
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:45,009
- Okay? Bye!
- Bye!

295
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:46,635
- Bye!
- Bye!

296
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:47,928
Your form's good!

297
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:51,265
I've actually been watching
some tutorial videos.

298
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:53,642
Oh, that explains it.

299
00:14:54,685 --> 00:14:57,646
Uh, do you maybe want to grab a bite?

300
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:58,856
- Yes!
- Oh!

301
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:00,900
- We do, we do!
- [SOFT LAUGH]

302
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:02,651
- You?
- We do, yes.

303
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:04,445
We do, right, Auntie?

304
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:05,654
- Okay…
- We'll go!

305
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,197
- [GIGGLES]
- All right.

306
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,574
[OLIVER GIGGLING]

307
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:15,998
Sir Eric!

308
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:18,667
- Hello!
- Oh, Oliver, who are you with?

309
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,753
[OLIVER] I'm with my auntie.
Auntie, this is Sir Eric.

310
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,671
Oh, Sir Eric!

311
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,007
- Nice to finally meet you.
- [OLIVER GIGGLES]

312
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:26,842
- Oh, nice to meet--
- Brandon, sir.

313
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:30,304
Oh, Sir Eric, you're quite
popular in our circle!

314
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:33,223
- Oliver always talks about you!
- [OLIVER LAUGHS]

315
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:35,184
Uh…

316
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:37,686
Sir Eric, are you here with someone?

317
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:40,773
If it's okay, can I sit with you?

318
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:42,316
[WHISPERS] My auntie's on a date--

319
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:43,651
- Hey! Shh!
- Oops…

320
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:44,902
[BOTH GIGGLING]

321
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:46,320
Sure, go ahead.

322
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:48,238
[PRECIOUS CHUCKLES LIGHTLY]

323
00:15:48,322 --> 00:15:50,532
- Be-- behave yourself.
- I will.

324
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,035
Thank you.

325
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:56,121
[OLIVER GIGGLES]

326
00:15:56,205 --> 00:16:02,378
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:04,338
Here.

328
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:05,923
- Here's your water.
- [THUDS]

329
00:16:06,006 --> 00:16:07,883
- Thank you!
- The waiters are busy.

330
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:09,468
- They are. [LAUGHS]
- Let's eat.

331
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:14,390
Hey, what are you doing?

332
00:16:14,473 --> 00:16:16,225
I'm taking a video of Auntie!

333
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:20,145
Are men banned in Angels of Grace?

334
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,398
[CHUCKLES] Not really.

335
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:24,191
If they're a relative, it's okay.

336
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:27,778
But staying there
is exclusively for women.

337
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:30,114
Oh, so…

338
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,866
does that mean I'm welcome
to pay you a visit?

339
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:35,869
[PRECIOUS LAUGHS] I said
it's just for relatives.

340
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:37,079
Ah…

341
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:38,872
Maybe as a future husband.

342
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:40,040
[BOTH GIGGLE]

343
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:41,417
- Psst!
- [WHISPERS] Oh!

344
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:44,211
[GIGGLES]

345
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:47,840
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

346
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:50,092
Do you think he's fit to be
a father figure to me?

347
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:52,678
Are you still looking for a father?

348
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:54,513
Of course!

349
00:16:54,596 --> 00:17:00,019
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,186
[OLIVER LAUGHS]

351
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:08,068
Caloy, I was able to get some money
to pay Ms. Tere.

352
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:10,487
I'll be able to open
my internet cafe again.

353
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:13,907
Huh? You're opening
your internet cafe again?

354
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,159
Don't you have a job already?

355
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:18,787
Seriously? Being a mere employee
won't make me rich.

356
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,122
Plus, didn't I tell you?

357
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:22,666
I need to surpass Billy.

358
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:23,834
All right.

359
00:17:24,334 --> 00:17:26,086
Who's going to look after your shop, then?

360
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,547
- Tell me.
- I'll hire someone.

361
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:31,175
Why hire someone else
when I'm here anyway?

362
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,134
Are you nuts?

363
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:34,261
I told you, we can't meet, right--

364
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:36,764
- Don't leave anything behind.
- Hey!

365
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:39,016
- Make sure you got everything.
- Hey, those are mine!

366
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:40,684
Where are you taking my computers?!

367
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:43,145
Oh! Ms. Tere sold them to us!

368
00:17:43,228 --> 00:17:45,439
She sold them? She can't do that!

369
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:47,900
I just talked to her just now!

370
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:49,735
I told her I'd settle my debts with her,

371
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:52,071
so those computers are mine!

372
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:54,239
It's too late. We've already bought them.

373
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:55,908
- Yes.
- [ABI] What?!

374
00:17:55,991 --> 00:17:57,493
W--wait a second.

375
00:17:57,576 --> 00:18:00,287
Marj, Charm, Toni, you…

376
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,914
What are you doing here?

377
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:04,249
How did you find this place?

378
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,918
Okay, we'll tell you.

379
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,878
But first, tell us this.

380
00:18:07,961 --> 00:18:10,422
How did you get our files on LoveFeast?

381
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,299
- Mm-hmm.
- LoveFeast?

382
00:18:12,382 --> 00:18:13,509
- [CHARM] Yes.
- Stole?

383
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:15,385
- [ABI] Me? I stole it?
- Yes.

384
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:16,345
- [CHARM] Mm-hmm.
- Huh?

385
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,305
What are you on? I didn't steal anything!

386
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:22,059
[ABI] Ms. Billy is too much.
She thinks that I stole it?

387
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:23,477
I didn't!

388
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,145
Don't just falsely accuse me!

389
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,772
False accusation?

390
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:27,856
Not at all!

391
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,067
We just really needed them
for a donation drive.

392
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,152
Yes, that's right!
We're going to donate them.

393
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:34,113
- Oh, for a donation.
- Yes!

394
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,448
Uh, give them back. Here.

395
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,784
Here. Here's my donation, money.

396
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:41,078
Take it. Give me my computers back.

397
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:42,204
No, thanks.

398
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,413
Huh?!

399
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:45,415
This is 40,000 pesos! It's a huge amount!

400
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:48,293
Sorry, it's not for sale!

401
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,670
- Yes, sorry!
- Sorry.

402
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:52,089
Well then, let's go, girls.
We might run late.

403
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:53,799
Not for sale, huh?

404
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,384
- [SHRIEKS]
- Hey, let go of her!

405
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:59,513
- That was 40,000 pesos!
- I told you, let go of her!

406
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:00,556
[ABI GRUNTS]

407
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:01,932
- Here, quick!
- Hey!

408
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:05,018
- Hey, what the hell?!
- Hold her!

409
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:06,019
- Ow!
- [ABI] Hey!

410
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:07,354
[ABI] My shoe-- Those are mine!

411
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:09,648
- [ABI] Help!
- Those are ours!

412
00:19:09,731 --> 00:19:12,568
- [ABI] Those are mine!
- [TONI] Let's go! A crowd is forming!

413
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:14,444
- Let's go!
- [CHARM GRUNTS]

414
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,904
- [ABI GROANS] Ow!
- Come on!

415
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:18,407
Let's go! They're here!

416
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,741
[ABI] Help!

417
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:22,327
Hey! Hey, those computers are mine!

418
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:26,039
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING, BANGING CAR]
- Help! Please help me!

419
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:28,250
- Those are my computers!
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

420
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:31,128
[ABI] Hey! Give them back!

421
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:32,838
- They're mine!
- [ENGINE REVVING]

422
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:35,465
Those are my computers!

423
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,384
Ugh!

424
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:39,595
[ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

425
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:41,847
[SCREAMS]
[EXHALES]

426
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,600
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [HORN HONKING IN DISTANCE]

427
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:47,519
[CHARM] Oh, man, it got crazy, but…

428
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,271
mission accomplished!

429
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:51,815
[ALL CHEERING]

430
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:54,318
You know, it was a good thing
that you thought of

431
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:56,195
- buying her computers.
- Mm-hmm.

432
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:58,238
She was absolutely infuriated!

433
00:19:58,822 --> 00:19:59,865
Toni…

434
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:02,201
What happened to you? Are you okay?

435
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:03,994
Oh, it's nothing.

436
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:06,205
What Abi got was worse!

437
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:08,665
- You should have seen her face!
- [LAUGHTER]

438
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:11,543
Yes, it was wild!
Like she was gonna bite us off!

439
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,503
- [GROWLS]
- Oh, it's nothing!

440
00:20:13,587 --> 00:20:14,880
That will teach her.

441
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:16,924
Let's see if she can pull
something like that again.

442
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:21,011
[TONI] <i>Plus, we didn't just get</i>
<i>her computers.</i>

443
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,304
Yes!

444
00:20:23,055 --> 00:20:24,640
- Ta-da!
- These, too!

445
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:26,099
[LAUGHTER]

446
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:31,063
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

447
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:38,237
'Bi. What happened to you?

448
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,571
What happened to your feet?

449
00:20:39,655 --> 00:20:41,949
I'm fine. [SNIFFLES]

450
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:43,659
Where are your computers?

451
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,827
What? Where'd they go?

452
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:49,790
They're all gone! All of them!

453
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:51,833
[ABI BREATHES DEEPLY]

454
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:54,920
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

455
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:57,839
Auntie Pres, this is really mine.
Mine is exactly like this.

456
00:20:57,923 --> 00:21:00,342
The brand name is fading,
and it has a scratch here.

457
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:03,512
That means that Abi is really dangerous!

458
00:21:03,595 --> 00:21:04,554
Be careful!

459
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:07,266
She even pretended
to be your fan just to rob you!

460
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:11,270
She did all that just for an idea
and a pair of shoes.

461
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:15,190
Just let her try doing that again.

462
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:17,109
I'm not going to back down.

463
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:21,989
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

464
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:24,491
- [BILLY]<i> Auntie Pres…</i>
<i>- </i>[PRECIOUS] <i>Yeah?</i>

465
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:25,909
<i>- You're all smiles here!</i>
<i>- So giddy!</i>

466
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:29,246
<i>- Who's this? That man you're with.</i>
<i>- Ah. That's Sir Eric.</i>

467
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:31,248
<i>But, apparently, you faked</i>
<i>your police clearance?</i>

468
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:32,249
<i>This is the original!</i>

469
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:33,750
<i>I really need a job.</i>

470
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,794
[LUCY] <i>You'll have to look</i>
<i>elsewhere. You're fired!</i>

471
00:21:35,877 --> 00:21:37,796
<i>- Oliver…</i>
<i>- Is Sir Eric here?</i>

472
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,589
[ENRICO] <i>I need to make</i>
<i>it up to my kids.</i>

473
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:41,300
[CALOY] <i>I love you this much.</i>

474
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:43,010
<i>You are permanently etched</i>
<i>onto my heart.</i>

475
00:21:43,093 --> 00:21:45,470
<i>Want me to get your shoes back? Huh?</i>

476
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,306
<i>Get my computers too</i>
<i>while you're at it.</i>

477
00:21:47,389 --> 00:21:49,766
<i>If only Ms. Tere hadn't</i>
<i>sold them to Billy.</i>

478
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:52,602
[BILLY] <i>And now that</i>
<i>the company is facing challenges,</i>

479
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:56,189
<i>is it right for them to be casualties</i>
<i>just to cut our losses?</i>

480
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:57,566
[CAMILLE] <i>Because the original idea</i>

481
00:21:57,649 --> 00:22:00,819
<i>came from the newest member</i>
<i>of the Pebblng family.</i>

482
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:02,612
<i>Oh, ma'am, thank you so much.</i>

483
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:05,907
<i>- Cheers!</i>
<i>- Cheers!</i>

484
00:22:05,991 --> 00:22:07,326
<i>You need this.</i>

485
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:08,744
<i>I missed this.</i>

486
00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:10,579
[BILLY] <i>Thank you.</i>

487
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:12,831
- [BILLY LAUGHS]
<i>- Cheers.</i>

488
00:22:13,790 --> 00:22:15,500
<i>You make it look so easy.</i>

489
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:16,752
<i>Being strong.</i>

490
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:17,919
<i>Composed.</i>

491
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:19,546
<i>I could say the same to you.</i>

492
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:22,215
<i>We got this.</i>

493
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:24,176
<i>We do.</i>
